WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.801
♪ (AMBIENT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:06.239
SPEAKER:<i> About 9:30,
I was by myself on the beach.</i>

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.476
<i> There was two people
 in the water already.</i>

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.379
<i> I heard screaming.</i>

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.349
<i> And I saw the blood.</i>

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.086
SPEAKER 2:<i> It seemed like
 more and more sharks</i>

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.187
<i>were arriving at Cape Cod
 each year,</i>

00:00:22.554 --> 00:00:24.991
<i> but not until
 the poor boy was killed</i>

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.093
did it really seem like, okay,
now they're here.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:30.863
SPEAKER 3:
<i>It's never quite been the same
 since the fatal attack.</i>

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.532
<i> It did cause a rift
 in the community.</i>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.669
This was a beautiful, young man
who lost his life

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.671
because we've been sitting,
doing nothing.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.641
SPEAKER 2:<i> Violence
can intersect any moment,</i>

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.742
<i>but one wouldn't have thought</i>

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.578
<i> on a sunny afternoon
off the coast of New England,</i>

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.514
<i> a shadow was waiting.</i>

00:00:48.747 --> 00:00:49.516
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:54.153
SPEAKER 4:
<i>It's easy to get caught up
in the</i> Jaws<i> angle to things...</i>

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:55.555
It was like this big around!

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.657
SPEAKER 4:<i> ...and take our eye
 off the bigger picture.</i>

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.859
<i> The research we're doing
 is really</i>

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.394
<i> to learn more
 about these animals,</i>

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.731
so that we can prevent
a bad interaction with a shark.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.665
-Got him.
-Yeah!

00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:09.035
SPEAKER 5:<i> Sharks,
they're attracted by the seals,</i>

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.202
and there are a lot of seals.

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.171
SPEAKER 6:<i> Because of that
Marine Mammal Protection Act,</i>

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.672
you can't touch 'em,
you can't look at 'em.

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.975
<i>You can't even yell at 'em
 as you go past 'em.</i>

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.878
SPEAKER 7:
<i>But there's something else
 going on down there.</i>

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:22.282
The waters warm,
so everything's marching north.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:27.086
Human activities
have imbalanced the ecosystem.

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.422
SPEAKER 8:
<i> We have a problem here,
 ladies and gentlemen,</i>

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:31.591
and the problem is man-made.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.294
SPEAKER 2:<i> We like to think
that our lives are orderly,</i>

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:37.429
but we don't find cooperation
from the natural world.

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:39.465
-Did you see that? A fin.
-(WHISTLE BLOWS)

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:40.934
SPEAKER 3:<i> Some of these people
 are acting like</i>

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.602
<i> the ocean's
 their little playground.</i>

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.337
Nah, it doesn't work that way.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.439
Went right in the damn
swimming area.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.043
Marine balance equation means
humans are part of the equation.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.045
SPEAKER 2:<i> Finding that balance
 is not easy.</i>

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:57.750
SPEAKER 3:
<i>Humankind must learn humility
 in the face of nature.</i>

